                <pb facs="0757" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg649"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carter to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hawaiian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is my sad duty to inform you that His
                    Majesty Kalakaua, King of Hawaii, died yesterday at 2:35 p.m., at San
                    Francisco.</p>
                <p>In this hour of personal grief and anxious solicitude for the welfare of my
                    bereaved country, I must content myself with this simple announcement of the
                    sorrowful event and pray you to communicate it to the President.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. A. P. Carter</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
